37,2,1,talk,May,,"It turns out the room is basically a private club for the people by the door! Plus, the desks are becoming a snack bar—the crumbs are everywhere.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The partition wall is just a single sheet of plasterboard. It's practically transparent to sound; you can hear every word of a phone call from the desks outside.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is interesting to see how the small things accumulate. I found that we spent a fair amount on outside hires for small groups, and our facilities team has been quite busy with the equipment rooms.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The fridge was a total disaster zone! Half the stuff had no owner, and someone had to clean it up three times! Also, we've been spending a lot of money on those outside rooms!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"It's a bit sad, actually. Since the sofa left, we only really chat by the printer. The new people barely know us, and almost nobody is using the room except the people by the door!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, exactly! It's like a VIP lounge for the door-sitters. And @Sakura, a disaster zone fridge? That sounds like a nightmare for whoever actually did the cleaning!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Servas, since the facilities team is so busy with equipment rooms, we should be careful about adding more technical gear to the break room. It might just lead to more callouts.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, Misaki. We must be careful not to create a burden for others. If we prioritize simplicity, we preserve the energy of those who keep our environment running. Balance is the key to a sustainable space.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@May, right? It was super gross! But the real mystery is the money! We're paying for outside rooms for just a few people. Why can't we just use our own room for that?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, that's a great point! If we're paying for other rooms, maybe it's because our room doesn't feel like a place where we can actually talk or hang out together? We need a spot where everyone feels welcome!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I totally agree. If only a couple of people are using it, it's not a ""shared"" room at all. It's just a convenient spot for the lucky few who sit by the door!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, it's not just about convenience. If the wall is that thin, the noise from the room disrupts the office, and the office noise disrupts the room. It's a problem for everyone.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are caught in a cycle where the physical space dictates our behavior. If the walls are thin and the room is neglected, we naturally seek refuge elsewhere, costing us both money and time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, if the wall is that thin, maybe that's why we're paying for those outside rooms! We can't have secret meetings if everyone can hear us, right? That's a total mystery solved!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! If we can't have a private chat without the whole office listening, it's no wonder we've become strangers. We need a place where we can actually be honest with each other!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"And let's not forget the crumbs! If we're just using it as a snack station and a private lounge, it's no wonder the cleaning falls on the same unlucky people. We need a real system!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"A system for cleaning is fine, but it won't fix the sound issue. If we want the room to be useful for everyone without disturbing the office, we have to address the noise first.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that any system we create should not become a chore that drains our spirit. Whether it is cleaning or soundproofing, the goal is to foster harmony, not to add more hours of labor to our days.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I agree! Let's make it a place where we can have fun and snacks without it being a mess! But we really have to stop spending all that money on outside rooms. It's like a treasure chest leaking coins!,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with everyone! We need a room that's not just clean and quiet, but a place where we can actually bond and talk about the hard stuff without feeling awkward. Let's make it a real home for the whole team!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
