62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A sounds like a recipe for more crumbs and fridge disasters! If we just leave it to ""whoever uses it,"" the same people will end up cleaning everything. I'm not a fan.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is the most logical choice. If the wall is as thin as I found, any other use will just be a constant distraction for those of us working right next to the door.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B offers a peaceful sanctuary, but I worry that Option C might lead to a cycle of administrative burdens. We must ensure the chosen path does not steal our precious time through endless upkeep.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Option C is the best! If we make it a meeting space, we can stop wasting all those coins on outside rooms! It's like getting a free room right next door!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C is great for the budget, but I'm worried it'll feel too formal. If it's just for ""meetings,"" will we ever actually just hang out and get to know each other?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, that's the problem! If it's just a ""meeting space,"" it's just more work. But Option B is too boring. I want a place where we can actually be social without it becoming a landfill!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, being social is fine, but not when it means the office becomes a noise chamber. Option B ensures that the people sitting by the door can actually focus on their work.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Misaki, your desire for focus is valid. However, we must consider if a Quiet Room simply pushes the noise and the ""walking about"" to other areas of the office, merely shifting the burden rather than resolving it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, but if we just make it a Quiet Room, we'll still be spending all that money on outside rooms! That's just silly! Option C lets us have our secret talks and save our treasure!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, you're right about the money, but I'm thinking about us! If we only use it for scheduled meetings, we'll still be strangers who only talk by the printer. We need a place for those unplanned, honest conversations!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I feel you, but ""unplanned"" usually means ""unmanaged."" If we go with Option A or C without a strict rule, we're just back to the door-sitters owning the place and someone else scrubbing the crumbs!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, unplanned conversations are exactly what cause the noise issues I mentioned. If we want a space that doesn't disrupt the office, we need a clear purpose that limits the volume. Option B is the only one that guarantees that.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, your concern for fairness is wise. If we choose a path that requires constant policing or cleaning, we risk creating a new kind of exhaustion. Perhaps a structured space is the most compassionate choice for all.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, but if we just stay quiet, we're still losing money every month! I saw the invoices, and it's a lot! Option C is like a magic trick that saves our budget and gives us a real place to talk!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, I understand the noise is a problem, but if we just stay quiet and separate, we'll never fix the fact that we're strangers! We need a space that encourages us to actually connect.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I love the spirit, but let's be real: ""connecting"" without a plan is how we got the crumb-covered desks. Option C is the only one with a calendar, which means actual accountability. I'm voting C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"Accountability is good, but a calendar doesn't soundproof a wall. Option C just formalizes the noise that disrupts our work. For the sake of the office environment, I'm voting for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance between the need for connection and the need for peace. However, to avoid the hidden costs of constant maintenance and the fatigue of unplanned labor, I believe a structured approach is best. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm voting for Option C too! We can't keep letting our money leak away on those outside rooms. Let's save our treasure and finally have a place for our secret meetings!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I really want us to be closer, but if everyone else is leaning toward C, I'll go with it too! As long as we use it to actually talk and not just for boring work, I'm happy. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
